    "title": "GBA vs GBC: Which Console Has Better Games?",
    "desc": "Comparing Game Boy Advance and Game Boy Color libraries. Which retro console wins?",
    "date": "2026-08-24",
    "category": "Comparison",
    "body": "<main style=\"max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px\">\r\n  <a href=\"/blog\" style=\"color:#c4a35a;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px\">← Back to Blog</a>\r\n  <span style=\"color:#555;font-size:12px;margin-left:12px\">2026-08-24</span>\r\n  <h1 style=\"font-size:2rem;margin:16px 0 8px\">GBA vs GBC: Which Console Has Better Games?</h1>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#aaa;margin-bottom:24px\">Comparing Game Boy Advance and Game Boy Color libraries. Which retro console wins?</p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">The Game Boy Advance and Game Boy Color are two of Nintendo's most beloved handhelds. Both have incredible game libraries. But which one is better? Let's break it down.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Graphics</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">The GBA wins here easily. It's essentially a portable SNES, with 32-bit graphics, mode 7 effects, and smooth animations. The GBC improved on the original Game Boy with color, but the sprites are still 8-bit.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Sound</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">GBA has significantly better sound. Stereo output, CD-quality music in some games, and the ability to produce complex sound effects. GBC had improved sound over the original, but it's still chiptune.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Game Library</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:12px\"><strong style=\"color:#c4a35a\">GBA highlights:</strong> Pokemon Emerald/FireRed/LeafGreen, Zelda: A Link to the Past, Metroid Fusion, Mario Kart, Castlevania: Aria of Sorrow</p>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\"><strong style=\"color:#c4a35a\">GBC highlights:</strong> Pokemon Gold/Silver/Crystal, Zelda: Link's Awakening DX, Super Mario Bros. Deluxe, Wario Land 3, Tetris DX</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">Backwards Compatibility</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">The GBA plays all GBC games, which is a huge advantage. You get two consoles in one. The GBC also plays original Game Boy games.</p>\r\n\r\n  <h2 style=\"font-size:1.3rem;margin:24px 0 12px;color:#c4a35a\">The Verdict</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"color:#ccc;margin-bottom:16px\">The GBA wins on technical merit — better graphics, sound, and a larger library. But the GBC has nostalgia and some of the best Pokemon games ever made. The good news? You can play both on <a href=\"/\" style=\"color:#c4a35a\">EggerMath</a>.</p>\r\r\n\r\n  <div style=\"margin-top:32px;padding:20px;background:#111;border:1px solid #1e1e22;border-radius:12px\">\r\n    <h2 style=\"font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px\">Play Both Libraries</h2>\r\n    <p style=\"color:#aaa;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:12px\">We have games from both GBA and GBC. Try them and decide for yourself.</p>\r\n    <a href=\"/\" style=\"color:#c4a35a;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700\">Browse All Games →</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n</main>",
